    {
      "id": "native-desktop-notify",
      "name": "Native desktop notifications (notify test|last|on|off, KDE Plasma etc)",
      "category": "ui",
      "status": "implemented",
      "since": "0.5.2",
      "note": "Sends notifications to the desktop's notification daemon (org.freedesktop.Notifications): via notify-send, falling back to a direct qdbus6/qdbus call, terminal bell always. 'notify test [text]' pops a test notification; 'notify last' re-sends the newest unread notification from the cache; 'notify on|off' toggles the persisted 'native_notify' switch (default on); the ui refresh command announces the notifications that arrived since the last refresh, tracking 'notify_seen_id'. Text is shell-quoted and cleaned (no newlines/control chars, length caps). 'notify daemon [--port N] [--bind IP]' runs the forwarding service (loopback by default) so notifications can be shown in ANOTHER user's desktop session: 'notify host <ip[:port]>' routes test/last and the refresh announcements through it; wire format is one line per notification (title TAB body). No authentication on the port, loopback by default. OPTIONAL systemd autostart: the Arch package ships /usr/lib/systemd/user/progressive-cli-notify.service (installed, not enabled) - 'systemctl --user enable --now progressive-cli-notify' starts the daemon with the desktop session; it listens on loopback and only forwards when a client sets 'notify host'. On Konsole/KDE the popups appear in the Plasma notification tray; the backend (notify-send or qdbus6) must be installed",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "src/matrix_commands.cpp",
        "pattern": "cmdNotify"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "demo-markdown",
      "name": "Demo markdown renderer (demo markdown)",
      "category": "ui",
      "status": "implemented",
      "since": "0.5.1",
      "note": "Renders the same sample the chat view uses. Supported: bold, italic (SGR 3), inline code, [text](url) as OSC 8 hyperlinks, #/##/### headers, bullets, - [x]/[ ] checkboxes, numbered lists, > quotes, fenced code blocks. Terminal realities: no font scaling exists, headers render bold; bold/italic need font faces (miss on many phone terminals); OSC 8 links are clickable only in OSC 8 terminals and in Konsole need profile Mouse 'Allow escape sequences for links' (+ optionally 'Open links by direct click'); the right-click Open Link item for OSC 8 links is unused upstream KDE gap (bug 520743, menued only for bare typed URLs); the click opens via the desktop default browser, so a dangling mimeapps default kills it (check gio mime x-scheme-handler/https); old emulators (VTE < 0.46.2, screen, tmux < 3.0) may strip the sequences",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "src/demo_repl.cpp",
        "pattern": "demoMarkdownShowcase"
      }
    },
